  "observations": [
    "On the fixed regression sets, adding the legacy beam to zenz+Qwen changes top1 by 0/1350 and +2/200; top5 by +5 and +4.",
    "Both added AJIMEE top1 hits are numeric-date cases with no validated zenz candidate. Post-hoc cached fallback analysis recovers them with legacy decode only on empty pools (15/1550 complete sentences); this is not a measured hybrid backend.",
    "Generated-only backends fail NIHONgo -> 日本ご among the four Shift probes. The full backend passes all four.",
    "Generated-only backends skip speculative pending-kana decoding. Real typing latency therefore compares complete backend policies, not identical partial-key features; pending timings are reported separately.",
    "Two Tatoeba first-choice changes involve the same candidates but batch-size-sensitive numerical scoring. Fresh full decoding reproduced all six disagreement cases and two control cases.",
    "GPU memory reports both active tensor peaks and allocator-reserved peaks for separate Japanese-only processes. It excludes CUDA context overhead and common Chinese models.",
    "The legacy kana model adds only about 89 MiB of loaded tensors; most extra peak GPU cost comes from constrained search, including provisional pending-kana expansions.",
    "No production default changed. The next integration candidate is generated zenz+Qwen for ordinary completed kana, with explicit-span and empty-pool fallback; it still requires end-to-end testing.",
    "Existing regression sets include examples used in prior debugging; these are not fresh blind-test results."
  ],
